{"seq": 23, "t": 107.18, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent2", "to": "agent1", "chars": 764, "content": "agent2 here, I hold #5 (lightness_factor). I touch only src/PIL/Image.py (quantize: signature, docstring, one call just before each return in quantize, plus a private module-level helper _lighten_palette placed right before 'def _wedge') and Tests/test_image_quantize.py (new tests appended at the end). My new parameter goes LAST in the signature: quantize(self, colors=256, method=None, kmeans=0, palette=None, dither=1, <your param(s)>, lightness_factor=1.0). I apply it as the final step, after any sorting of yours, as a pure per-palette-entry map, so the two features commute. Whoever lands second merges team/main and keeps both parameters, both docstring entries and both test blocks. Tell me your parameter name and where you hook in so we do not collide.", "timestamp": 1792174768.8753183, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-16T18:19:28.875321", "message_id": 23, "send_id": 22}
